## Facts
- Round 1 changed `src/Zlink.Framework/Runtime/Channels/ZLinkClientServerClientRuntime.cs` so
  `ReconnectAsync` waits for the Disconnected/Closed monitor edge of the fenced physical connection
  before re-registering the endpoint (replacing the fixed 100 ms delay), then loops `Connect`. Alone:
  5/5 and class 35/35 green.
- Supervisor full-suite gate v5 (`--filter 'FullyQualifiedName!~CanonicalActorJoinIngressReplyTests'`,
  `--no-build`, log
  `/tmp/claude-1000/-home-hep7-project-zlink/be443aad-d720-4c23-9860-099f913fdfd4/scratchpad/gate-v5-rest.log`)
  fails it again at 00:03:22 into the run:
  `System.TimeoutException : Expected raw record was not received. diagnostics=manual:tcp://127.0.0.1:26345=protocol:pushed-control;generation=2;attempt=3;admissionStarted=True;admissionCompleted=False;reconnect=False;current=False; physical=1; ready=0`
  i.e. reconnect finished (`reconnect=False`), admission attempt 3 on generation 2 started, but
  `ready=0` / `current=False`: the reconnected pair never became ready (no ConnectionReady for the
  new physical connection) so the admission request never got a reply. So the round-1 fix is
  incomplete: it is load/ordering-sensitive. The gate v4 failure (before round 1) had the same shape.
- Candidate mechanisms to check against the Core socket spec (`core/doc/spec/core/socket/README.ko.md`
  connect/disconnect/reconnect semantics; `07-router`, DEALER endpoint identity; monitor event
  ordering) and the binding: (a) `Disconnect(endpoint)` followed by `Connect(endpoint)` after the
  Disconnected edge — but Core may still hold the endpoint's reconnect entry (the session's own
  reconnect timer) and dedupe the second `Connect` as the same endpoint, so no new pipe/ready event
  is ever produced; (b) the Disconnected event observed belongs to a *different* physical generation
  (an earlier close), so re-registration still races the retiring pipe; (c) the ready event for the
  new pipe arrives but is attributed to the old generation and dropped by the fence
  (`FencePhysicalConnection`) — check `ready=0` accounting vs. the generation checks around
  `:1018-1033` and the ConnectionReady handler; (d) the test's server side (pushed-control malformed
  frame path) closes the *server* pipe and the client's reconnect lands before the server re-accepts.
  Decide with a trace, not by guessing: add a temporary file sink for the framework debug log / monitor
  events (remove before finishing) and record the exact event sequence (generation, event type,
  endpoint, timestamp) in the failing run.
- Reproduce under load: the test passes alone. Run `--filter 'FullyQualifiedName~ClientServerChannelRuntimeTests'`
  while 6 background `yes > /dev/null` hogs run (kill them afterwards), 5×; or run the class
  concurrently with `--filter 'FullyQualifiedName~StatefulServiceRuntimeTests'` in a second process
  (both need the flock — see below — so use the hog approach first). If you cannot reproduce in 5×,
